# Disassembly annotations for "Street Fighter II NE (DEMO by Parisoft)".
# Format (one directive per line; BB:AAAA in hex; K:address = kernel common to the 3 code banks):
#   label   BB:AAAA Name                 routine or table name
#   ram     AAAA Name [N]                RAM variable name (N = number of bytes; default 1)
#   comment BB:AAAA text                 end-of-line comment
#   block   BB:AAAA text                 block comment before the address (repeat for multiple lines)
#   code    BB:AAAA                      force disassembler to treat as code
#   data    BB:AAAA-BBBB                 force to treat as data
#   table   BB:AAAA split lo=AAAA hi=BBBB n=N delta=1    split jump table (stores address-1, used with RTS)
#                                        (tables in the lda/pha/lda/pha/rts pattern are detected on their own)
#   table   BB:AAAA words n=N            16-bit pointer table
#   ramcode BB:AAAA TAM ORG              chunk copied to RAM and executed there
#   statebank BB frames=BB from=AAAA to=AAAA   fighter state bank (7-byte header + 14-byte frames)
#   statecond BB:AAAA n=N             state machine condition table (split lo/hi, RTS trick,
#                                        stores address-1): target labels become the names printed in
#                                        "; -- STATE" headers of the fighter data bank
#   ptr     BB:AAAA lo|hi BB:TTTT        this immediate instruction (or data byte) is the low/high half of a pointer
#                                        to BB:TTTT. Only for cases the trace missed (tools/ptr_candidates.py).
#   imm     BB:AAAA EXPRESSION           manually write the immediate operand (e.g. imm 3F:F8BF <FarCall)
#                                        (pointers to ROM seen in the trace already come out symbolic on their own)
#   alt     SYMBOL BB:AAAA TAM           alternative code (following lines starting with "|"), assembled only with
#                                        -D SYMBOL; without the symbol the original is emitted. Used for optional fixes.
#   patch   BB:AAAA XX XX ...            overwrites bytes of the reference image before analysis/emission (data
#                                        new or fixes that must enter the canonical build; does not cross banks).
#   keepbank BB                          bank kept by hand (not generated): only guarantees the segment in sf2ne.cfg.
#   ram AAAA Name N   names N consecutive bytes: Name, Name+1, ... (vectors, P1/P2 pairs).

ramcode 3F:F935 14 049E


# ============================================================================================================
# KERNEL (code repeated at $FC7C-$FF9A in banks $37, $3B and $3F)
# ============================================================================================================
label K:FC7C IrqHandler
block K:FC7C ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
block K:FC7C IRQ = MMC5 scanline counter ($5203/$5204). Produces raster effects.
block K:FC7C   IrqStage ($03FF) = 0      -> first fight split: end of HUD, stage begins
block K:FC7C   IrqStage > 0              -> subsequent fight splits; the last does the floor line by line (parallax)
block K:FC7C   IrqStage < 0 (bit 7)      -> menu screens (selection / VS / quote): swaps CHR by band
block K:FC7C CAUTION: the wait loops (dex/bne, nop) are cycle-counted. Touching here misaligns the image.
label K:FC8E Irq_FightNext
label K:FCB6 Irq_FloorLine
comment K:FCB6 one pass per scanline of the floor: own horizontal scroll (FloorScrollX table)
label K:FD04 Irq_FightArmNext
label K:FD0E Irq_SetLine
label K:FD16 Irq_Exit
label K:FD1C Irq_FightFirst
label K:FD62 Irq_Menu
label K:FD8C Irq_MenuLast
comment K:FD97 human player only (FighterIsCpu = 0)
comment K:FDDF same for player 2 — never executed in the demo (P2 is always CPU)
label K:FE14 MenuSplitLine
label K:FE18 MenuSplitChrA
label K:FE1B MenuSplitChrB
label K:FE1E NmiHandler
block K:FE1E ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
block K:FE1E NMI (vblank): sends OAM, runs the current screen mode task (ScreenMode), fixes the CHR banks
block K:FE1E of the two fighters' sprites, scrolling and PPU registers, and signals the main loop.
comment K:FE5A frame counter
comment K:FE5E tells the main loop that vblank has passed
label K:FE66 NmiDispatch
label K:FE71 NmiTaskLo
label K:FE79 NmiTaskHi
label K:FE82 NmiTask_Intro
label K:FE8B NmiTask_Title
label K:FE9C NmiTask_Select
label K:FEBA NmiTask_Fight
label K:FEC5 NmiTask_VsQuote
label K:FED8 PaletteUpload
block K:FED8 Copies the palette buffer (PaletteBuf, 24 colors = 8 palettes x 3; color 0 of all is $0F) to the PPU.

# ============================================================================================================
# BANK $3F — reset, main loop, fight engine core
