# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 3 P2 naming batch: last automatic code labels of bank $3F (engine core).
# Named by role demonstrated by code; labels only, no byte change.
label 3F:E158 TransAnimTimerSet
comment 3F:E158 TransAnimTimerSet — in TransApply: hit/reaction frame -> FighterAnimTimer = 1
label 3F:E15D TransNextPtrSet
comment 3F:E15D TransNextPtrSet — in TransApply: writes next state pointer (FighterNextPtrLo/Hi)
label 3F:E191 CondOpponentAttackClass
comment 3F:E191 CondOpponentAttackClass — in CondOpponentAttacks: opponent class (reaction/hit/projectile)
label 3F:E1CA CondFarBackFacing
comment 3F:E1CA CondFarBackFacing — in CondOpponentFarBack: returns turn bit ($40)
label 3F:E1E0 CondNearAbsDiff
comment 3F:E1E0 CondNearAbsDiff — in CondOpponentNear: normalizes X difference sign
label 3F:E1E6 CondNearLimit
comment 3F:E1E6 CondNearLimit — in CondOpponentNear: compares |dx| with $21
label 3F:E239 CondGrabAbsDiff
comment 3F:E239 CondGrabAbsDiff — in CondCanGrab: normalizes X difference sign
label 3F:E252 CondGrabOpponentClass
comment 3F:E252 CondGrabOpponentClass — in CondCanGrab: opponent class ($30-$A8)
label 3F:E2A3 CondRoundLostFalse
comment 3F:E2A3 CondRoundLostFalse — in CondRoundLost: false path (RoundResult = this fighter or $FF)
label 3F:E2B3 AnimNextStateCheck
comment 3F:E2B3 AnimNextStateCheck — in AnimAdvance: is there a next state chosen? (FighterNextPtrHi)
label 3F:E2D8 AnimStatePtrSet
comment 3F:E2D8 AnimStatePtrSet — in AnimAdvance: writes new state and new frame pointers
label 3F:E2F0 AnimStateClassSet
comment 3F:E2F0 AnimStateClassSet — in AnimAdvance: applies new frame class (StateSetByte)

# TEMPORARY (Ken): skips warning/QR screens to speed up manual test. 18 NOPs instead of
# 18-byte farcall, so kernel still starts at $FC7C. TODO: remove this patch so warning/QR reappears.
patch 3F:F828 EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA EA
comment 3F:F83A ScreenTitle
comment 3F:F86C ScreenPlayerSelect
comment 3F:F87E ScreenVersus
comment 3F:F890 Match
comment 3F:F8A2 ScreenWinQuote
comment 3F:F85E no character chosen
comment 3F:F866 P1 = human
comment 3F:F86A P2 = CPU
label 3F:F8B7 InstallFarCall
imm 3F:F8BF <FarCall
imm 3F:F8C3 >FarCall
comment 3F:F8B7 copies 20 bytes of FarCallRom to $049E
label 3F:F8E7 JoyPollBoth
label 3F:F8F1 JoyPollSafe
block 3F:F8F1 Reads controller A (0/1) until two reads match — protects against DMC channel corruption.
block 3F:F8F1 Result in JoyState,x ; JoyPrev,x gets previous state.  (same idea as joy_poll_safe from familib)
label 3F:F91C JoyRead
label 3F:F935 FarCallRom
label 3F:E5AC RandomSeed
label 3F:E5B9 Random
label 3F:E03D DistanceX
comment 3F:E03D A = |x of P2 - x of P1|
label 3F:E049 DistanceY
label 3F:E000 HitFreeze_E000
comment 3F:E000 freezes the hit fighter: saves movement/velocities/timer in ram_0312-031C and stops at current frame for $0E frames
label 3F:E0CE StateCheckTransitions
block 3F:E0CE ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
block 3F:E0CE FIGHTER STATE MACHINE (data-driven; data is in FighterStateBank at $A000).
block 3F:E0CE Walks the transition list: each node is a 7-byte state header — +0 condition number
block 3F:E0CE (Cond* below; >= $80 = unconditional), +1/+2 next alternative (chained list), +3/+4 next
block 3F:E0CE state in natural chain, +5 class, +6 hit count. The first true condition applies THIS
block 3F:E0CE NODE as next state (FighterNextPtr = node address; AnimAdvance enters it).
block 3F:E0CE zp_DD marks search origin: $04 = GuardRedirect, $02 = button move, $01 = special move.
block 3F:E0CE With zp_DD = $04 and class $28/$30: skips first node when it is the current state.
block 3F:E0CE With zp_DD = $02 and class $70-$98 and node != current state: skips first node. And with bit 2 of class cleared
block 3F:E0CE and CondOpponentFarBack: skips first node too (does not react from behind).
label 3F:E129 TransNextNode
comment 3F:E129 false condition: goes to node +1/+2 and repeats search (pointer 0 = end of list, nothing changes)
label 3F:E13B TransApply
comment 3F:E13B true condition: current node becomes next state; AnimTimer=1 in hit/reaction classes ($28-$40/$B0-$E0) unless frame has flag bit 3
label 3F:E168 StateCondDispatch
label 3F:E171 StateCondLo
label 3F:E17D StateCondHi
statecond 3F:E171 n=12
comment 3F:E171 12 conditions; each entry stores address-1 (RTS trick with pha/pha/rts)
label 3F:E189 CondOpponentAttacks
comment 3F:E189 true if I am standing/crouching (class & 3) AND opponent is in reaction class ($70-$98), hit class ($B0-$E0) or has projectile in air (his)
label 3F:E1B1 CondOpponentFarBack
comment 3F:E1B1 true if opponent is at |dx| >= $0F and I have my back to him: returns $40 (bit 6 of FighterFlip) to turn, 0 if facing or close
label 3F:E1D6 CondOpponentNear
comment 3F:E1D6 true if |dx| < $21
label 3F:E1ED CondStanding
comment 3F:E1ED bit 0 of class = standing posture
label 3F:E1F3 CondCrouching
comment 3F:E1F3 bit 1 of class = crouching posture
label 3F:E1F9 CondInAir
comment 3F:E1F9 true if FighterY < FloorY (above ground)
label 3F:E204 CondOnGroundOrVelX
comment 3F:E204 true if FighterY = FloorY or VelX/VelXSub != 0 (on ground or sliding)
label 3F:E212 CondInputDown
comment 3F:E212 true if InputDir = $08/$0B/$0C (straight down or diagonal-down); returns InputDir itself
label 3F:E224 CondProjectileFree
comment 3F:E224 true if this fighter's projectile slot is free (his zp_7B = 0)
label 3F:E22E CondCanGrab
comment 3F:E22E |dx| < $18, both on ground, InputDir = forward/back ($05/$06) and opponent class < $30 or $50-$9F (turn states $A0-$A9 don't count, nt)
label 3F:E271 CondVictory
comment 3F:E271 true if RoundResult = this fighter AND opponent is down (class >= $F0) AND no projectiles in air AND voice channel is free
label 3F:E296 CondRoundLost
comment 3F:E296 true if RoundResult != this fighter AND RoundResult != $FF (round ended; applies to draw)
label 3F:E2A6 AnimAdvance
block 3F:E2A6 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
block 3F:E2A6 ONE ANIMATION STEP (every frame, before collision test):
block 3F:E2A6  - current frame effect $0B -> fires projectile (ProjLaunch, param = frame +5)
block 3F:E2A6  - FighterNextPtr != 0 -> enters new state chosen by TransApply: writes class (+5) and
block 3F:E2A6    hits (+6), first frame = node + 7. Special case: state $49 with zp_62 != 0 uses the
block 3F:E2A6    alternative +1/+2 of current state. Frame effect $20 -> sound effect (SfxPlay).
block 3F:E2A6  - no next state and ram_031C != 0 -> restores movement frozen by hit-freeze.
block 3F:E2A6  - otherwise advances frames: +11 (loop repeats) > 0 -> decrements and branches to +14/+15;
block 3F:E2A6    zero -> +12/+13 (next frame); +12/+13 = 0 -> StateAdvance (natural chain +3/+4;
block 3F:E2A6    class $30 with HP <= pending damage uses +1/+2, i.e. cuts to damage state).
block 3F:E2A6  - air KO (HP <= pending damage, above ground): HitStop = $78 and KO voices.
label 3F:E301 FreezeRestore
comment 3F:E301 returns velocities/timer saved by hit-freeze (ram_0312-031C)
label 3F:E3B8 FrameEnter
comment 3F:E3B8 first frame entry of new state: loads zp_44 with loop repeats (frame +11)
label 3F:E3BF FrameEnterCommon
comment 3F:E3BF any frame entry: movement (+8), writes FramePtr, effect (+5/+6), AnimTimer (+0), flags (+7)
label 3F:E371 StateAdvance
comment 3F:E371 end of animation: passes to state +3/+4 of header (natural chain); class $30 with HP <= pending damage uses alternative +1/+2
label 3F:E47F StateSetByte
block 3F:E47F Writes state byte (header +5) to FighterState and triggers state class sound:
block 3F:E47F classes $70-$98 -> sound effect (bank $37), classes $A0-$E0 -> fighter voice (VoicePlayFighter).
comment 3F:E3B1 header +6 (hit count)
label 3F:E4C2 MoveVelSetup
comment 3F:E4C2 dispatches by frame movement mode (+8): 0/1 absolute, 2/3 acceleration, 4/5 subpixel
label 3F:E4DA MoveVelAbs
comment 3F:E4DA modes 0/1: frame VelX/VelY (+9/+10) are the new velocity, directly
label 3F:E4F1 MoveVelSubpixel
comment 3F:E4F1 modes 4/5: frame velocity divided by 16 — integer in VelX and remainder<<4 in VelXSub
label 3F:E53C MoveVelAdd
comment 3F:E53C adds signed vel/16 to current velocity (VelX, VelXSub and VelY)
label 3F:E597 MoveVelAccel
comment 3F:E597 modes 2/3: accelerates with MoveVelAdd (mode bit 0 does not change effect)
label 3F:E837 ProjLaunch
comment 3F:E837 A = speed ($00/$01/$02, step in ProjSpeedStepTbl): born at FighterX +/- $27, direction = FighterFlip (bit 6 of ProjFlags)
label 3F:E854 ProjUpdate
comment 3F:E854 moves 1/16 of step per subframe; Y = FloorY - $27; dies outside $0C-$FB
label 3F:E8BB ProjClash
comment 3F:E8BB two projectiles at |dx| < $18: both get bit 7 of ProjFlags and die after 16 steps
label 3F:E8F1 ProjHitTest
comment 3F:E8F1 projectile AABB (point +/- $0C/$0B) against opponent's body boxes
label 3F:E941 ProjHit
comment 3F:E941 projectile hit: dies, reaction class $CB, damage $6C and calls damage routine
label 3F:EBA3 LoadHitBoxesBoth
comment 3F:EBA3 processes fighter 1 then 0 (called by FightersUpdate)
label 3F:EBA5 LoadHitBoxes
comment 3F:EBA5 maps collision bank at $8000; frame record +3/+4: body boxes 1/2 and attack box (h = 0 absent), mirrored by FighterFlip, attack clamped at $20/$E0
label 3F:ECF1 HitTest
comment 3F:ECF1 attack box of X vs body 1/2 of Y: one hit per frame (zp_3E), exhausts AttackHitsLeft
label 3F:E974 InputClear
comment 3F:E974 zeroes fighter input (neutral direction, no attack/hold); runs every frame outside active fight (ScreenMode != 5 or round already decided)
comment 3F:E984 zeroes recognizer command 0 step (CmdMotionStep,x = list entry 0)
comment 3F:E986 zeroes command 0 window (CmdMotionWin,x)
comment 3F:E988 overflow: CmdMotionStep+1,x is NOT entry 1 (interleaved arrays) — hits 1 byte of neighbor
comment 3F:E98A same overflow in window; entries 1-5 are never zeroed here, only expire by window
label 3F:E963 DirCodeTbl
comment 3F:E963 controller bits -> direction code (bit 0 forward, 1 back, 2 down, 3 up): $04 neutral, $05 forward, $06 back, $07 up, $08 down, $09-$0A up diagonals, $0B-$0C down diagonals
label 3F:F799 GuardClassTbl
comment 3F:F799 guard class byte by direction (index InputDir-$04): $29 standing, $2A crouching
label 3F:F671 InputDispatch_F671
comment 3F:F671 player input: triggers state transition — direction (frame flag bit 2), button (bit 1) or special (bit 0); next state class ($58-$68 accepts direction) decides what passes
label 3F:F6F5 TransViaTbl
comment 3F:F6F5 reads state table pointer and calls transition walker
label 3F:F704 GuardRedirect
comment 3F:F704 in guard ($28-$2F): switches to defense of current direction (GuardClassTbl) and received hit (table ram_032A), preserving frame and timer
label 3F:E7D2 AiUpdate
block 3F:E7D2 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
block 3F:E7D2 CPU AI. Two levels: (1) a native "think" routine, specific to each character
block 3F:E7D2 (AiCharRoutine -> character bank, ex. RyuAiThink at $00:8F46), which chooses a script;
block 3F:E7D2 (2) a script interpreter (bytecode, opcodes $80-$91 = AiOp00..AiOp11) that generates commands.
label 3F:E7A4 AiCallCharRoutine
label 3F:E6E6 AiCharRoutine
comment 3F:E6E6 one entry (address-1) per character; only Ryu exists
label 3F:E6E8 AiStartScriptNow
comment 3F:E6E8 A/Y = script pointer; always starts
label 3F:E6F3 AiStartScript
comment 3F:E6F3 A/Y = script pointer; only starts if Random&7 < AiLevel (otherwise hesitates)
label 3F:E6FE AiDoNothing
comment 3F:E70A AiLevel = 7 (fixed in MainLoop): CPU reacts 7 out of 8 chances — that's why AI seems "too hard"
comment 3F:F84C AI level (0..7). It's the only place that sets difficulty
label 3F:E82D AiOpDispatch
label 3F:E6C2 AiOpLo
label 3F:E6D4 AiOpHi
label 3F:E5DF AiOp00
label 3F:E5EA AiOp01
label 3F:E5F7 AiOp02
label 3F:E604 AiOp03
label 3F:E61A AiOp04
label 3F:E61F AiOp05
label 3F:E62A AiOp06
label 3F:E62D AiOp07
label 3F:E636 AiOp08
label 3F:E63E AiOp09
label 3F:E646 AiOp0A
label 3F:E659 AiOp0B
label 3F:E65C AiOp0C
label 3F:E6B0 AiOp0D
label 3F:E686 AiOp0E
label 3F:E69B AiOp0F
label 3F:E6B3 AiOp10
label 3F:E6BE AiOp11
label 3F:E98D InputUpdate
block 3F:E98D ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
block 3F:E98D HUMAN PLAYER INPUT: reads JoyState and feeds command recognizer (special moves).
block 3F:E98D This is where the reported "hard hadouken / delayed command" problem lives (and in CmdStep*).
label 3F:E99A InputButtons
block 3F:E99A Buttons A (punch) and B (kick) with two strength levels on one button:
block 3F:E99A   short press (released before 7 frames)  -> WEAK hit, emitted ONLY WHEN RELEASED
block 3F:E99A   held 7 frames or more                -> STRONG hit, emitted EVERY frame from 7th to 20th, and again on release
block 3F:E99A InputAttack,x receives: 0 weak punch, 1 strong punch, 2 weak kick, 3 strong kick, $FF nothing.
block 3F:E99A Consequence: every hit comes out delayed (at least until button release) and strong repeats — see docs/BUGS.md.
block 3F:E99A FIX_EDGE_ATTACK adjustment (adjustment section at end of file): weak on rising edge + promotion to strong.
comment 3F:E9A7 passed 20 frames holding: ignores
comment 3F:E9AB less than 7 frames: hasn't decided yet (waits for release)
comment 3F:E9AD counter < 7: goes to button B without emitting anything
comment 3F:E9AF 7..20 frames holding: strong punch, every frame
label 3F:E9B4 BtnAReleased
comment 3F:E9B4 A released: zeroes punch counter and emits weak (if held <7) or strong again
label 3F:E9C0 EmitWeakPunch
comment 3F:E9C0 weak punch emitter (A=$00): output of quick release (<7 frames)
comment 3F:E9C2 released: <7 frames = weak (0), else strong (1)
label 3F:E9CB BtnBCheck
comment 3F:E9CB button B (kick) processing; A's "nothing to do" cases fall here
label 3F:E9E5 BtnBReleased
comment 3F:E9E5 B released: zeroes kick counter and emits weak/strong
label 3F:E9F1 EmitWeakKick
comment 3F:E9F1 weak kick emitter (A=$02): output of quick release (<7 frames)
label 3F:E9FC BtnNone
comment 3F:E9FC no active button: InputAttack = $FF
label 3F:E9FE InputSetAttack
label 3F:EA01 InputDirection
comment 3F:EA01 d-pad -> direction code relative to side fighter faces (table DirCodeTbl)
label 3F:EA24 InputCommands
comment 3F:EA24 recognizer: zp_D7/D8 = character special list (fiche slot 8, ram_033E/0340), zp_DA/zp_DB = JoyState/JoyPrev mirrored by FighterFlip, zp_DC = fighter, zp_D9 = list position
label 3F:EA58 CmdWalkLoop
comment 3F:EA58 key = list[zp_D9], bit 7 = end of list ($FF); dispatches CmdStep[key] with Y = key
comment 3F:EA60 x += 2 per list entry: x = fighter + 2*position indexes interleaved CmdMotionStep/CmdMotionWin arrays (even = P1, odd = P2)
label 3F:EA6A CmdStepDispatch
comment 3F:EA6A jumps to CmdStep[key] via CmdStepLo/CmdStepHi (address-1 + RTS), Y = key $00-$12
label 3F:EA73 CmdWalkEnd
comment 3F:EA73 end of list: recovers x = fighter (zp_DC) and returns
label 3F:EA76 CmdStepLo
label 3F:EA89 CmdStepHi
comment 3F:EA89 19 keys: $00-$07 and $10 motion (EB4B), $08-$0D charge (EA9C), $0E/$0F 3x button (EAFD), $11 A+B together (EB32), $12 empty (EB4A)
label 3F:EA9C CmdStepCharge
block 3F:EA9C ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
block 3F:EA9C CHARGE, 3 phases: hold direction for $3C (60) frames, release pressing release direction
block 3F:EA9C (next sequence byte) in an 8-frame window, then required button in same window. (nt)
label 3F:EAAD CmdChargeHold
comment 3F:EAAD phase 0: charge direction pressed -> counts frames (saturates at $3C); released before 60 -> zeroes
label 3F:EAC4 CmdChargeReset
comment 3F:EAC4 zeroes step and window of current command
label 3F:EACB CmdChargeTick
comment 3F:EACB holding: frame counter, saturates at $3C (60)
label 3F:EAD4 CmdChargeRelease
comment 3F:EAD4 phase 1: release direction pressed in 8-frame window (EAF8 decrements on each error)
label 3F:EAE1 CmdChargeButton
comment 3F:EAE1 phase 2: required button (CmdKeyAttackTbl[key] == InputAttack) -> CmdMoveIdx[fighter] = list position
label 3F:EAF8 CmdChargeWinTick
comment 3F:EAF8 window expired (< 0) -> zeroes command
label 3F:EAFD CmdStepMash
comment 3F:EAFD 3x the SAME button (CmdKeyAttackTbl[key] == InputAttack), intervals up to 8 frames. (nt)
label 3F:EB0C CmdMashCount
comment 3F:EB0C correct press: counts (1..2), zeroes interval
label 3F:EB1A CmdMashDone
comment 3F:EB1A 3rd press -> CmdMoveIdx[fighter] = list position
label 3F:EB21 CmdMashReset
label 3F:EB28 CmdMashGap
comment 3F:EB28 interval between presses passed 8 -> zeroes
label 3F:EB32 CmdStepBothBtn
comment 3F:EB32 A+B pressed together on rising edge (now $C0, before not) -> CmdMoveIdx[fighter] = list position. (nt)
label 3F:EB4A CmdStepNone
comment 3F:EB4A key $12: empty slot; its 4 sequence bytes (E0AF-E0B2) are CmdKeyAttackTbl — harmless
label 3F:EB4B CmdStepMotion
block 3F:EB4B ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
block 3F:EB4B DIRECTION SEQUENCE: Y = key*4 + step. A step counts when required bit is pressed AND
block 3F:EB4B some direction is NEW (pressed now, absent in previous frame) — holding still does not advance.
block 3F:EB4B $0C (12) frame window between steps; byte $00 ends sequence -> button phase (another 12).
label 3F:EB69 CmdMotionWinTick
comment 3F:EB69 no new direction / required bit released: counts window; passed 12 -> zeroes command
label 3F:EB73 CmdMotionAdvance
comment 3F:EB73 step done: zeroes window, advances step; CmdMotionTblNext,y (SAME y) reads NEXT byte — $0 falls into button phase already
label 3F:EB7F CmdMotionBtnWin
comment 3F:EB7F button phase: same 12-frame window
label 3F:EB88 CmdMotionButton
comment 3F:EB88 required button (CmdKeyAttackTbl[key] == InputAttack) -> CmdMoveIdx[fighter] = list position; zeroes command
label 3F:EB9C CmdMotionReset
label 3F:E067 CmdMotionTbl
comment 3F:E067 sequencias dos golpes especiais, 4 bytes por chave $00-$11 (bits do controle: 04 baixo, 01 frente, 02 tras, 08 cima, 80 A, 40 B; $00 encerra)
label 3F:E068 CmdMotionTblNext
comment 3F:E068 CmdMotionTbl+1: lido em EB73 com o MESMO indice para ver o proximo byte da sequencia sem iny
label 3F:E0AF CmdKeyAttackTbl
comment 3F:E0AF botao exigido por chave, 17 bytes ($00-$10): 0 soco fraco, 1 soco forte, 2 chute fraco, 3 chute forte
label 3F:E0C0 CmdKeyListRyu
comment 3F:E0C0 lista de especiais do Ryu (chaves, $FF = fim): hadouken ch $02/$03 (chute), shoryuken $06/$07 (chute), tatsumaki $04/$05 (soco); a POSICAO na lista vira CmdMoveIdx
comment 3F:E0C7 segunda lista (chaves de carga $08-$0D) para outro personagem — nenhum ponteiro da ficha aponta aqui hoje
label 3F:EF74 FightersUpdate
block 3F:EF74 Um quadro de logica da luta: atualiza os dois lutadores (alternando a ordem a cada quadro) e desenha.
label 3F:EF99 FighterUpdate
comment 3F:EFC1 CPU or human?
comment 3F:EFC5 CPU -> AI
comment 3F:EFCB human -> control


# --- rotinas e continuacoes nomeadas na revisao de documentacao (ordem de endereco) ---
label 3F:E357 AnimAdvanceEnter
comment 3F:E357 enters a frame whose pointer comes in A (lo) and next byte (hi), in AnimAdvance loop branches
label 3F:E701 AiStartScriptCheck
comment 3F:E701 common part of AiStartScript*: bit 6 of zp_DD always starts; otherwise draws Random&7 against AiLevel
label 3F:E74C AiDefaultGuard
comment 3F:E74C AI step: in neutral state holds back (guard) and exits; otherwise decides or continues script
label 3F:E7E7 AiScriptLoop
comment 3F:E7E7 script loop: $FF ends; otherwise decodes opcode and copies operands
label 3F:E7FE AiScriptCopyArgs
comment 3F:E7FE copies positive operands to zp_6D.. until next opcode (negative)
label 3F:E82B AiOpRun
comment 3F:E82B Y = opcode read; falls into AiOpDispatch
label 3F:E89F ProjUpdateStore
comment 3F:E89F writes ProjX if inside $0C-$FB and counts step; otherwise kills projectile
label 3F:EC45 LoadBoxBody2
comment 3F:EC45 reads body box 2 (height 0 = absent), mirrored by FighterFlip
label 3F:EC92 LoadBoxAttack
comment 3F:EC92 reads attack box (height 0 = absent), clamped at $20-$E0
label 3F:ECE7 LoadBoxesNext
comment 3F:ECE7 end of boxes: reloads for fighter 0 or arms HitTest (x=1 attacks y=0)
label 3F:ED6C HitTestApply
comment 3F:ED6C hit: passes EffectParam and hit fighter (Y) to damage routine
label 3F:ED7A HitTestNext
comment 3F:ED7A swaps roles (0 attacks 1) and repeats HitTest; otherwise ends
label 3F:ED83 HitDamageApply
comment 3F:ED83 applies damage: if target is in compatible guard, blocks; otherwise adds pending damage
label 3F:EE27 HitDamageHeavy
comment 3F:EE27 damage >= $20: zeroes state, arms HitStop=$78 and chooses heavy reaction
label 3F:EE4E HitDamageReact
comment 3F:EE4E chooses damage reaction (HitReactClass) and corresponding state
label 3F:EEC2 HitDamageSfx
comment 3F:EEC2 plays damage sound effect and indexes reaction table
label 3F:EEDF HitDamageTrans
comment 3F:EEDF loads state bank and applies damage transition (zp_DD=4)
label 3F:EEF7 HitDamageKO
comment 3F:EEF7 damage kills: converts reaction class to KO state
label 3F:EFCE FighterUpdateExec
comment 3F:EFCE executes fighter X entry and animation (InputDispatch + AnimAdvance)
label 3F:EFF8 HitRecoverTick
comment 3F:EFF8 counts HitStop and, when done, restores fighter's next state
label 3F:F033 GrabCheck
comment 3F:F033 checks grab: fighter X grabs Y if in state $A0-$A8 and aligned
label 3F:F037 GrabCheckOne
comment 3F:F037 tests X's grab on Y and applies displacement/state
label 3F:F09B JoyPollBothSel
comment 3F:F09B reads both controllers in selection (JoyPollSafe 0 and 1)
label 3F:F0A5 MoveDispatch_F0A5
comment 3F:F0A5 dispatches movement application by MoveMode (table MoveApplyDispatchLo/Hi)
label 3F:F0BD MoveOpponentRel
comment 3F:F0BD mode $00: positions X relative to opponent (X = opponent X +/- VelX)
label 3F:F0F2 MoveAbsolute
comment 3F:F0F2 mode $01: applies VelY and VelX directly (absolute movement)
label 3F:F156 MoveAbsLeft
comment 3F:F156 absolute mode: applies displacement to the left
label 3F:F194 MoveAbsLeftFwd
comment 3F:F194 absolute mode to the left with camera advance/retreat
label 3F:F1C0 MoveScrollCamera
comment 3F:F1C0 applies camera displacement and passes it to other objects
label 3F:F204 MoveScrollOthers
comment 3F:F204 moves opponent and projectile along with camera
label 3F:F225 MoveApplyX
comment 3F:F225 applies displacement to FighterX and zeroes VelX
label 3F:F236 MoveAir
comment 3F:F236 mode $02/$03: integrates VelY with gravity and ground
label 3F:F279 MoveAirScroll
comment 3F:F279 integrates VelY subpixel (air displacement)
label 3F:F2C0 MoveAirScrollApply
comment 3F:F2C0 applies air displacement and adjusts ground/opponent
label 3F:F317 MoveAirGravity
comment 3F:F317 applies gravity ($30 per frame) and tests ground
label 3F:F332 MoveAirGround
comment 3F:F332 in air: moves horizontally and applies friction on landing
label 3F:F377 MoveHorizontal
comment 3F:F377 mode $04/$05: applies VelX with corner rules
label 3F:F3FB MoveHorizLeft
comment 3F:F3FB horizontal movement to the left (per FighterFlip)
label 3F:F453 MoveHorizLeftFwd
comment 3F:F453 horizontal movement to the left with camera advance
label 3F:F49A MoveScrollStage
comment 3F:F49A applies stage displacement and moves camera
label 3F:F512 MoveScrollStageOthers
comment 3F:F512 moves opponent and projectile along with stage
label 3F:F533 MoveHorizApply
comment 3F:F533 applies horizontal displacement to FighterXSub/FighterX
label 3F:F543 MovePushApart
comment 3F:F543 if fighters overlap, pushes each half of invasion
label 3F:F5B5 MovePushApply
comment 3F:F5B5 applies push to FighterX
label 3F:F5C5 MoveClampEdges
comment 3F:F5C5 starts X clamp at screen edges
label 3F:F5CD MoveClampX
comment 3F:F5CD locks X at $20-$E0 and saves overflow
label 3F:F621 MoveClampNext
comment 3F:F621 passes to other fighter for clamp
label 3F:F62C MoveClampPush
comment 3F:F62C adds clamp overflow to opponent's X (push through victim)
label 3F:F648 MoveGrabEscape
comment 3F:F648 escape grab: hit-freeze, zeroes reaction class and plays sound

# --- tabelas do nucleo de luta (projetil, impacto, knockback e despachos de movimento) ---
label 3F:E055 HitSfxTbl
comment 3F:E055 hit sfx by attacker class (6 bytes; only 0..2 used)
label 3F:E05B ProjSpawnYOffsetTbl
comment 3F:E05B projectile birth Y: FloorY - $27 (2 bytes used)
label 3F:E05E ProjSpeedStepTbl
comment 3F:E05E projectile step by speed ($17/$25 for speed 0/1)
label 3F:E064 ProjSpawnXOffsetTbl
comment 3F:E064 projectile birth delta X: FighterX +/- $27 (2 bytes used)
label 3F:E4CE MoveVelDispatchLo
label 3F:E4D4 MoveVelDispatchHi
comment 3F:E4CE movement mode dispatch in MoveVelSetup: address-1 by MoveMode (absolute/acceleration/subpixel)
label 3F:EF06 KnockbackXGroundTbl
comment 3F:EF06 knockback X by reaction class, victim standing/crouching (PostProc)
label 3F:EF13 KnockbackXAirTbl
comment 3F:EF13 knockback X by reaction class, victim neutral/in air (RoundStart2)
label 3F:EF20 KnockbackYGroundTbl
comment 3F:EF20 knockback Y by reaction class, victim standing/crouching (PostProc)
label 3F:EF2D KnockbackYAirTbl
comment 3F:EF2D knockback Y by reaction class, victim neutral/in air (RoundStart2)
label 3F:EF3A KnockdownReactTbl
comment 3F:EF3A new reaction class when accumulated knockback knocks victim down
label 3F:EF47 KOReactTbl
comment 3F:EF47 new reaction class on KO (indexed by class & $1F)
label 3F:F0B1 MoveApplyDispatchLo
label 3F:F0B7 MoveApplyDispatchHi
comment 3F:F0B1 movement application dispatch: address-1 by MoveMode (relative/absolute/air/horizontal)

# ============================================================================================================
# BANK $3B — fight (rounds, HUD, drawing), VS screens and final quote, video utilities
# ============================================================================================================
label 3B:E000 FighterLoadChar
block 3B:E000 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
block 3B:E000 Loads the fighter "fiche" FighterChar,x from bank $3C tables (10 characters per table):
block 3B:E000 data banks (frames at $8000, states at $A000) and pointers to basic states.
block 3B:E000 Today only column 0 (Ryu) is filled. For a new character, this is the starting point.
block 3B:E000 In RAM pointers are split in half: lo at ram_031E+x, hi at ram_0320+x — P1 = (031E,0320), P2 = (031F,0321).
block 3B:E000 Detail: only slot 0 hi is read WITHOUT ,y (lda D3C_800A, E025) — character != 0 would inherit Ryu's hi.
label 3B:E098 FighterRoundInit
comment 3B:E098 initial position: P1 x=$5A, P2 x=$A6, y=$CD (ground)
label 3B:E1F6 PortraitBuild
label 3B:E3BE PpuUnRle
block 3B:E3BE Decompresses RLE (NESlib/Shiru format: 1st byte = marker; marker,n = repeats last byte n times;
block 3B:E3BE marker,0 = end) directly to PPUDATA. Input: A = low byte, X = high byte of data address.
label 3B:E426 FadeOut_Bank3B
label 3B:E4D6 FadeIn
label 3B:E844 NmiFightVram
label 3B:EA61 ScreenVersus
label 3B:EC1B ScreenWinQuote
label 3B:ED81 DrawFighters
label 3B:EDD9 DrawFighter
label 3B:F2DF OamHideRest
comment 3B:F2DF hides unused sprites this frame (Y = $FE from OamIndex to end)
label 3B:F2EA DrawMetasprite
block 3B:F2EA Draws a metasprite (list of 8x16 sprites) in OAM. Data at (zp_D9): attribute, then groups
block 3B:F2EA "quantity, dx, dy, tiles..." until a negative byte. zp_DB/zp_DC = base position, zp_DD = mirrored.
label 3B:F551 Match
block 3B:F551 ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
block 3B:F551 THE ENTIRE FIGHT: rounds until someone closes the match.
label 3B:F556 RoundStart
label 3B:F58E FightFrame
block 3B:F58E One-frame fight loop: waits vblank, sound, round rules, split screen, fighter logic.
comment 3B:F5B2 "hit stop": while HitStop not zero, logic runs every other frame
label 3B:F60F RoundInit
label 3B:F64F RoundLogic
label 3B:F68B RoundTimerTick
comment 3B:F68B clock decreases 1 every 32 frames
comment 3B:F6A0 time out: compares both energies
label 3B:F6D0 RoundIntroStep
comment 3B:F6FD voice 0 = "ROUND"
comment 3B:F82E voice 6 = "YOU"
comment 3B:F841 voice 7 = "WIN"
comment 3B:F853 voice 9 = "PERFECT" (human winner with full energy, $58)
comment 3B:F86F voice 8 = "LOSE" (winner is CPU)
comment 3B:F823 RoundResult: 0 = P1 won, 1 = P2 won, 2 = draw, $FF = fight in progress
comment 3B:F709 voices 1..3 = round number
comment 3B:F717 voice 5 = "FIGHT"
label 3B:F7E1 RoundEndStep
label 3B:F908 StageSplitSetup
label 3B:F940 StageParallaxCalc
label 3B:FACB DrawSupportScreen
label 3B:FADC DrawTitleScreen
