# ============================================================================================================
# BANK $04 — Ken frames/metasprites/collision (original data) + AI stub
# ============================================================================================================
# Ken AI stub (this delivery's CPU remains Ryu). Ken's fiche points to $90E0.
# There are 8 scripts, like Ryu's table at $00:8E72, and all lead to the $FF terminator, so that
# no pointer falls into collision data.
patch 04:90E0 F0 90 F0 90 F0 90 F0 90 F0 90 F0 90 F0 90 F0 90
table 04:90E0 words n=8
block 04:90E0 Ken AI stub (this delivery's CPU remains Ryu).
block 04:90E0 Ken's fiche points here ($90E0). There are 8 scripts, like Ryu's table at $00:8E72,
block 04:90E0 and all lead to the $FF terminator, so that no pointer falls into collision data.
# Layout of Ken's defeat portrait. On defeat, PortraitBuildP1 uses DE=3, but Ken's normal layout
# Ken ($8A59) has only 2 groups; reading the next byte ($8A92, metasprite $8A91 attribute) as
# count $00 triggers 255 iterations and overflows portrait buffer (the "broken photo").
# Solution: copy normal layout to free space and add a third empty group.
# Byte $90F0 remains $FF (terminator of AI stub above); layout starts at $90F1.
patch 04:90F1 10 00 06 00 AF 08 0A 0C 0E 10 12 06 00 BF 14 16
patch 04:9101 18 1A 1C 1E 06 00 CF 20 22 24 26 28 2A 04 00 DF
patch 04:9111 2C 2E 30 32 04 00 EF 34 36 38 3A 80 00 02 20 DF
patch 04:9121 00 02 02 20 EF 04 06 80 00 80
comment 04:90F1 Ken defeat portrait layout: copy of normal + empty group 3 (DE=3)

